'The source equation can be cleared of denominators and interpreted algebraically. Its transcendence consequence is strong only when all coefficients are independently algebraic. Coefficients defined from the same unknown solution do not meet that hypothesis.',
['For v>0 consider e^v=(C₁²/4)v²+(1+2C₁D)+4D²/v². Set T=C₁v/2+2D/v, so the right side is 1+T².','Assume C₁ and D are algebraic real numbers when invoking the algebraic-number consequence. They may instead be endogenous in the historical model, in which case that consequence is conditional.'],
