['Let R:D→R² be continuously differentiable. A nonsingular Jacobian at a zero gives local uniqueness by the inverse function theorem.','Let G map a closed interval J into itself and satisfy |G(s)−G(t)|≤q|s−t| with q<1. Such a scalar reduction is an additional global structure, not a consequence of local invertibility.'],
